<!--
  The Dodo mark: one continuous stroke that swells through the middle and tapers to a point at
  both ends — speech as a single unbroken ribbon rather than yet another microphone.

  It is a filled outline, not a stroke, so the thickness can vary: the path runs left-to-right
  along the top edge, then back right-to-left along the bottom edge offset by 2.2 units, and the
  two edges meet at the tips where the offset falls to zero.
-->
